    "gatheredBy": "load-sport-data, the 2025 MLS Cup playoffs as played, from Wikipedia's playoffs page: a fixed bracket of nine seeds a conference, the 8 and 9 seeds meeting in the wild card round for the 1 seed's place. Round one is a best-of-three series, one match here: its score is games won (a drawn game went straight to penalties, and its shoot-out winner took the game), scheduled at game 1, and its home side is team 1, the higher seed, who hosted games 1 and 3. Every other round is one game hosted by the higher seed, MLS Cup included, its score after extra time with its shoot-out, and its half-time score from the goal minutes; a series has none. Kickoffs are the page's local times. Seeds are the conference seeds; rankings are the overall table (Real Salt Lake 19th). ESPN's scoreboards agree on the conference semifinals, conference finals and MLS Cup, and on Vancouver's shoot-out over LAFC; ESPN lists Philadelphia v New York City at 00:45Z, and the file keeps the page's 7:30 pm EST. Odds to win are made up by ranking.",
